WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.676
Imagine keeping every receipt in a shoebox. To know how you are doing, you would have to sort the whole box. A tidy notebook, written up every day, answers the question at once.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:26.160
A full set of accounting records means every transaction is recorded by double entry, in the books of prime entry and the ledgers. Incomplete records keep only some of this.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:43.392
Full records bring many benefits. Statements can be prepared at any time. The owner makes better decisions. Customers and suppliers can be controlled. A trial balance can be drawn up, and banks trust the figures.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:52.145
First, give the number of reasons asked for, usually two. State each reason clearly, in one phrase.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:01:01.972
Then develop each reason with because, or so that, to show its effect. The point earns one mark. The development earns the second.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:18.977
Here is a real question from June 2024. Thelma, a sole trader, kept only incomplete records. Discuss two reasons why a business should maintain full accounting records. Four marks.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:31.338
First reason: with full records, Thelma could produce financial statements whenever she needs them, even every month. Because the figures are already in the books, nothing has to be pieced together.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:45.268
Second reason: full records help the owner make better decisions, since she is working from complete, current figures, not guesses. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:56.586
A common mistake is listing reasons without developing any. A list earns only the identification marks.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:01.002
Another is writing the same reason twice in different words.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:09.786
Now you try. Give Priya two developed reasons. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:24.041
Reason one: she can control her receivables. She will know exactly what each café owes, so she can chase late payments and keep cash coming in.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:33.587
Reason two: a bank is more likely to lend to her, because complete records give it reliable figures to judge her business.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:42.485
Remember: state each reason, develop it with because or so that, and make the reasons different. Now try the practice questions.
